[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hazelgrove/hazel/pulls/2222","id":3567704390,"node_id":"PR_kwDOBMdeZM7UptlG","html_url":"https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/2222","diff_url":"https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/2222.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/2222.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hazelgrove/hazel/issues/2222","number":2222,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Incremental evaluation","user":{"login":"Negabinary","id":31668468,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNjY4NDY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31668468?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Negabinary","html_url":"https://github.com/Negabinary","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Negabinary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Negabinary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Negabinary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Negabinary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Negabinary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Negabinary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Negabinary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Negabinary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Negabinary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Working on a formalism at https://typst.app/project/r1zZKHltWXXBRyJcVkTc5k.\r\nEverything up to \"The Tuple Bottleneck\" is proven and implemented in Hazel. \r\n\r\n<img width=\"596\" height=\"250\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c00da9d4-5faa-4432-a986-4e5ae5e1463b\" />\r\n\r\nDuring evaluation, this pr \"freezes\" any parts of the previous evaluation that haven't changed, and re-uses the values.\r\n\r\nYou can turn on some visual \"ice\" to show which sub-expressions are frozen by toggling \"Incremental Reuse\" in the nut menu.\r\n\r\nThe evaluator is passed a map of the previous evaluation at each top-level id. It is able to re-use an expression iff:\r\n\r\n1. **The call stack is empty** (This is our notion of top-level)\r\n2. **The elaboration has not changed** (Uses deep equality; every id in the program is checked at most once, so this check is quadratic in the length of the program)\r\n3. **The co-context does not contain any dirty variables** (Variables are dirtied if the thing they are bound to has changed)\r\n4. **The ids associated with the co-context has not changed since last time**\r\n5. **The probe targets in the sub-expression have not changed**","created_at":"2026-04-22T14:12:05Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T22:00:06Z","closed_at":"2026-05-19T18:24:16Z","merged_at":"2026-05-19T18:24:16Z","merge_commit_sha":"d2e85b38010c8eb9e3ce650404a73e718d084d4b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hazelgrove/hazel/pulls/2222/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hazelgrove/hazel/pulls/2222/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hazelgrove/hazel/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hazelgrove/hazel/issues/2222/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hazelgrove/hazel/statuses/7aa51ee0eeadf048361a5275dea03e53146dddf0","head":{"label":"hazelgrove:incremental-evaluation","ref":"incremental-evaluation","sha":"7aa51ee0eeadf048361a5275dea03e53146dddf0","user":{"login":"hazelgrove","id":18447820,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE4NDQ3ODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18447820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hazelgrove","html_url":"https://github.com/hazelgrove","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hazelgrove/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hazelgrove/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haz